			"Message": "docs(Rest): Expand README with dual-compiler architecture and comprehensive documentation\n\nSignificantly expand and refine the Rest README to accurately reflect the project's role as the unified compilation API server for the Land ecosystem, correcting the earlier post-rebrand description that still underspecified the compiler backend architecture.\n\nKey additions and improvements:\n- Add mission-focused blockquote articulating the compilation server value proposition\n- Rewrite Overview to present Rest as the dual-compiler (OXC + SWC) orchestration layer with interchangeable pipelines\n- Expand Key Features to document both compiler backends, ESBuild bundling, NLS endpoints, compilation workers, and watch mode\n- Update Architecture Principles table with Dual Compiler Strategy principle and specific Struct/ and Fn/ component references\n- Remove `&#x2001;` emoji entity spacing from Mermaid diagram labels in favor of plain spaces for better rendering compatibility\n- Add comprehensive consumer integration table to \"In the Land Project\" documenting Maintain, Cocoon, Land Web App, and Air consumers plus Common dependency\n- Add Getting Started section with key dependencies table (oxc_*, rayon, tokio, clap, notify, Common)\n- Add Security section documenting type safety, memory safety, input validation, and compiler sandboxing layers\n- Update Compatibility and Related Documentation sections with complete target and reference lists\n- Reorganize project structure tree entries to consistently list sub-modules in alphabetical+logical order\n\nThis brings the Rest documentation into parity with the actual codebase structure and compiler architecture, serving as an authoritative reference for contributors and consumers.",
			"SHA": "7eebd3e4c768505f24f00693672d41ddd560133c"
		},
